{"id":"ws2-mn95","title":"saccānurakkhaṇā","titleEn":"Protecting the Truth","ref":"MN 95 · excerpt","source":"Pāḷi Workshop booklet","credit":"Pāḷi text and English translation as in Mor’s Pāḷi Workshop booklet.","section":"extra","collection":"workshop","group":"2 · sammāvācā","groupSub":"Right Speech","paras":[{"t":[["“"],["pañca","pañca"],[" "],["kho","kho"],[" "],["ime","ime"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["dhammā","dhammā"],[" "],["diṭṭh’eva","diṭṭh’eva"],[" "],["dhamme","dhamme"],["\n"],["dvedhā","dvedhā"],[" "],["vipākā","vipākā"],["."],[" "],["katame","katame"],[" "],["pañca","pañca"],["?"],["\n"],["saddhā","saddhā"],[","],[" "],["ruci","ruci"],[","],[" "],["anussavo","anussavo"],[","],[" "],["ākāra-parivitakko","ākāra-parivitakko"],[","],["\n"],["diṭṭhi-nijjhāna-kkhanti","diṭṭhi-nijjhāna-kkhanti"],["."],[" "],["ime","ime"],[" "],["kho","kho"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],["\n"],["pañca","pañca"],[" "],["dhammā","dhammā"],[" "],["diṭṭh’eva","diṭṭh’eva"],[" "],["dhamme","dhamme"],[" "],["dvedhā","dvedhā"],[" "],["vipākā","vipākā"],["."]],"en":"“There are five things, Bhāradvāja, that may turn out in\ntwo different ways here and now. What five?\nFaith, liking, oral tradition, logical reasoning,\nand reflective acceptance of a view. These five things may\nturn out in two different ways here and now.","lines":true},{"t":[["api","api"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["susaddahitaṃyeva","susaddahitaṃyeva"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[","],["\n"],["tañ","tañ"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["rittaṃ","rittaṃ"],[","],[" "],["tucchaṃ","tucchaṃ"],[","],[" "],["musā","musā"],[";"],["\n"],["no","no"],[" "],["ce’pi","ce’pi"],[" "],["susaddahitaṃ","susaddahitaṃ"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[","],["\n"],["tañ","tañ"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["bhūtaṃ","bhūtaṃ"],[","],[" "],["tacchaṃ","tacchaṃ"],[","],[" "],["anaññathā","anaññathā"],["."]],"en":"Now something may be fully accepted out of faith,\nyet it may be empty, hollow, and false;\nbut something else may not be fully accepted out of faith,\nyet it may be factual, true, and unmistaken.","lines":true},{"t":[["api","api"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["surucitaṃyeva","surucitaṃyeva"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["…"],[" "],["pe","pe"],[" "],["…"],["\n"],["svānussutaṃyeva","svānussutaṃyeva"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["…"],[" "],["pe","pe"],[" "],["…"],[" "],["suparivitakkitaṃyeva","suparivitakkitaṃyeva"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],["\n"],["…"],[" "],["pe","pe"],[" "],["…"],[" "],["sunijjhāyitaṃyeva","sunijjhāyitaṃyeva"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[","],[" "],["tañ","tañ"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["rittaṃ","rittaṃ"],[","],["\n"],["tucchaṃ","tucchaṃ"],[","],[" "],["musā","musā"],[";"],[" "],["no","no"],[" "],["ce’pi","ce’pi"],[" "],["sunijjhāyitaṃ","sunijjhāyitaṃ"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[","],["\n"],["tañ","tañ"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["bhūtaṃ","bhūtaṃ"],[" "],["tacchaṃ","tacchaṃ"],[" "],["anaññathā","anaññathā"],["."]],"en":"Again, something may be liked very much …\nwell transmitted … well cogitated …\nwell reflected upon, yet it may be empty, hollow,\nand false; but something else may not be well reflected\nupon, yet it may be factual, true, and unmistaken.","lines":true},{"t":[["saccam","saccam"],[" "],["anurakkhatā","anurakkhatā"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["viññunā","viññunā"],[" "],["purisena","purisena"],["\n"],["n’ālam","n’ālam"],[" "],["ettha","ettha"],[" "],["ek’aṃsena","ek’aṃsena"],[" "],["niṭṭhaṃ","niṭṭhaṃ"],[" "],["gantuṃ","gantuṃ"],[":"],["\n"],["‘"],["idameva","idameva"],[" "],["saccaṃ","saccaṃ"],[","],[" "],["mogham","mogham"],[" "],["aññan’”ti","aññan’”ti"],["."]],"en":"[Under these conditions] it is not proper for a wise man\nwho protects truth to come to the definite conclusion:\n‘Only this is true, anything else is wrong.’”","lines":true},{"t":[["“"],["kittāvatā","kittāvatā"],[" "],["pana","pana"],[","],[" "],["bho","bho"],[" "],["gotama","gotama"],[","],[" "],["sacc’ānurakkhaṇā","sacc’ānurakkhaṇā"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[","],["\n"],["kittāvatā","kittāvatā"],[" "],["saccam","saccam"],[" "],["anurakkhati","anurakkhati"],["?"],[" "],["sacc’ānurakkhaṇaṃ","sacc’ānurakkhaṇaṃ"],["\n"],["mayaṃ","mayaṃ"],[" "],["bhavantaṃ","bhavantaṃ"],[" "],["gotamaṃ","gotamaṃ"],[" "],["pucchāmā”ti","pucchāmā”ti"],["."]],"en":"“But, Master Gotama, in what way is there the protection\nof truth? How does one protect truth?\nWe ask Master Gotama about the protection of truth.”","lines":true},{"t":[["“"],["saddhā","saddhā"],[" "],["ce’pi","ce’pi"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["purisassa","purisassa"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[":"],["\n"],["‘"],["evaṃ","evaṃ"],[" "],["me","me"],[" "],["saddhā’ti","saddhā’ti"],[" "],["—"],[" "],["iti","iti"],[" "],["vadaṃ","vadaṃ"],[" "],["saccam","saccam"],[" "],["anurakkhati","anurakkhati"],[","],["\n"],["na","na"],[" "],["tveva","tveva"],[" "],["tāva","tāva"],[" "],["ek’aṃsena","ek’aṃsena"],[" "],["niṭṭhaṃ","niṭṭhaṃ"],[" "],["gacchati","gacchati"],[":"],["\n"],["‘"],["idameva","idameva"],[" "],["saccaṃ","saccaṃ"],[","],[" "],["mogham","mogham"],[" "],["aññan’ti","aññan’ti"],["."]],"en":"“If a person has faith, Bhāradvāja, he protects truth when\nhe says: ‘My faith is thus’;\nbut he does not yet come to the definite conclusion:\n‘Only this is true, anything else is wrong.’","lines":true},{"t":[["ettāvatā","ettāvatā"],[" "],["kho","kho"],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[" "],["sacc’ānurakkhaṇā","sacc’ānurakkhaṇā"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[";"],["\n"],["ettāvatā","ettāvatā"],[" "],["saccam","saccam"],[" "],["anurakkhati","anurakkhati"],[";"]],"en":"In this way, Bhāradvāja, there is the protection of truth;\nin this way he protects truth;","lines":true},{"t":[["ettāvatā","ettāvatā"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[" "],["mayaṃ","mayaṃ"],[" "],["sacc’ānurakkhaṇaṃ","sacc’ānurakkhaṇaṃ"],[" "],["paññapema","paññapema"],[";"],["\n"],["na","na"],[" "],["tveva","tveva"],[" "],["tāva","tāva"],[" "],["sacc’ānubodho","sacc’ānubodho"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],["."]],"en":"in this way we describe the protection of truth;\nbut as yet there is no awakening to truth.","lines":true},{"t":[["ruci","ruci"],[" "],["ce’pi","ce’pi"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["purisassa","purisassa"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["…"],[" "],["pe","pe"],[" "],["…"],["\n"],["anussavo","anussavo"],[" "],["ce’pi","ce’pi"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["purisassa","purisassa"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["…"],[" "],["pe","pe"],[" "],["…"],["\n"],["ākāra-parivitakko","ākāra-parivitakko"],[" "],["ce’pi","ce’pi"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["purisassa","purisassa"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[" "],["…"],[" "],["pe","pe"],[" "],["…"],["\n"],["diṭṭhi-nijjhāna-kkhanti","diṭṭhi-nijjhāna-kkhanti"],[" "],["ce’pi","ce’pi"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["purisassa","purisassa"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[":"],["\n"],["‘"],["evaṃ","evaṃ"],[" "],["me","me"],[" "],["diṭṭhi-nijjhāna-kkhantī’ti","diṭṭhi-nijjhāna-kkhantī’ti"],[" "],["—"],["\n"],["iti","iti"],[" "],["vadaṃ","vadaṃ"],[" "],["saccam","saccam"],[" "],["anurakkhati","anurakkhati"],[","],["\n"],["na","na"],[" "],["tveva","tveva"],[" "],["tāva","tāva"],[" "],["ek’aṃsena","ek’aṃsena"],[" "],["niṭṭhaṃ","niṭṭhaṃ"],[" "],["gacchati","gacchati"],[":"],["\n"],["‘"],["idameva","idameva"],[" "],["saccaṃ","saccaṃ"],[","],[" "],["mogham","mogham"],[" "],["aññan’ti","aññan’ti"],["."],["\n"],["ettāvatā","ettāvatā"],[" "],["kho","kho"],[","],[" "],["bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],[","],[" "],["sacc’ānurakkhaṇā","sacc’ānurakkhaṇā"],[" "],["hoti","hoti"],[","],["\n"],["ettāvatā","ettāvatā"],[" "],["saccam","saccam"],[" "],["anurakkhati","anurakkhati"],[","],["\n"],["ettāvatā","ettāvatā"],[" "],["ca","ca"],[" "],["mayaṃ","mayaṃ"],[" "],["sacc’ānurakkhaṇaṃ","sacc’ānurakkhaṇaṃ"],[" "],["paññapema","paññapem